[{'criterion': 'The response cites at least two specific examples of research where more sunlight or vitamin D led to better health outcomes (e.g., for COVID patients (Association Between Vitamin D and COVID-19–Related Outcomes: An Umbrella Review of Meta-Analyses), for autoimmune system compromised patients (The Schematic Assessment of Vitamin D Deficiency in Relation to Autoimmune Disorders and Its Implications in Internal Medicine), for pregnant people (The Effects of Vitamin D Supplementation During Pregnancy on Maternal, Neonatal, and Infant Health: A Systematic Review and Meta-analysis), depressed people (Nutritional interventions in depression: The role of vitamin D and omega-3 fatty acids in neuropsychiatric health).).', 'weight': 3.0, 'axis': 'References & Citation Quality'}
